  "hypothesis": "A stable byte-wise radix index sort removes the quadratic, skew-sensitive insertion loops; cache-aligned private histograms and disjoint stable scatters should scale its large passes on four ARM64 cores while preserving strcmp order.",
  "notes": "Zero-padded record storage makes the fixed-width byte passes match strcmp for any token fitting its declared field; stdout remains sequential.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
